const context = $input.first().json.context;
const system = `You classify one ecommerce product question before drafting a reply. First split the question into every independent clause, including requests joined by and, commas, or then. Return JSON only with: clauses (array of text, intent, status), intents (1-6 unique keys selected only from supported_intents), customer_language (ISO 639-1), country_code (explicit destination only or null), event_date (explicit date in YYYY-MM-DD; resolve a month/day to the next occurrence using current_date), requested_currency, requested_language, requires_private_reply, unmatched_requests, summary. Every independent customer request must map to an intent or unmatched_requests. Multiple labels for one underlying request do not create additional independent requests. A request to see different color options is one customer goal even if both color-availability and color-photo labels apply. Never invent facts. Preserve ambiguous customer wording: a broad alteration question does not establish custom sizing, a particular design change, or whether the customer means before purchase or after delivery. Use request_other_customization when no specific alteration is supplied; never invent the requested change. Distinguish product attributes, fit, size chart, plus size, stock, restock, tracking, cancellation policy, actual photos, color photos, and customization intents exactly. Existing-order status, tracking, and refunds are private. Use ask_pockets for whether the item includes pockets and request_add_pockets when the customer asks whether pockets can be added. A combined pockets question may select both. Use request_custom_color only when the customer asks to manufacture an unlisted/custom color; use ask_available_colors for whether a listed color is available. Use request_remove_train for shortening or removing a train. Do not use request_custom_length unless the customer explicitly asks to change the garment length.`;
