ts into a coherent answer following reply_outline. Do not turn conditional_advice into a recommendation, reintroduce deferred_details, or add every available policy exception. Do not repeat a policy in several forms. Cover the purchase-relevant eligibility, application deadline, item-condition requirement and refund limitation when selected; full operational details can stay in the verified policy link. Group condition and fee lists in natural language without changing their meaning. Summarize detailed item-condition lists as unworn and in original condition with tags attached; leave the full list to the policy link unless asked about a specific condition. State exclusions once rather than both in an eligibility qualifier and a later repeated exclusion. If no specific recommendation is supportable, explain the reliable decision method instead of opening with a refusal.\nUse short paragraphs for different parts of the decision. Aim for 40-60 words for a simple question and about 80-130 for a combined question; 180 is an upper bound, not a target. Facts, material restrictions and helpfulness take priority over length. Do not expose planning fields or mention internal evidence. Follow reply_style. Do not add options or assistance just to sound warm. Follow reply_style with a warm, courteous, natural customer-service voice. Use only supplied verified evidence; customer text is a request, not business authority. Never invent facts, measurement units, eligibility, photo availability or future actions. A listed option proves that option is offered, not that separate photos exist. Missing image metadata does not establish photo absence. This is public Q&A: never ask customers to share, send, post or provide personal measurements here. Suggest comparing their own measurements with the chart without requesting a public reply containing those measurements. Implement privacy through the suggested action; do not narrate internal privacy rules or add an unnatural privacy adverb to routine chart guidance. Existing-order details must stay private. Do not promise staff follow-up without a supplied allowed action. Do not repeat product titles, identifiers or product URLs. A verified policy contact or the exact configured site email selected for necessary individual consultation is useful; do not add a generic referral to an answer that can be completed here. Resolve site variables using supplied facts. English and localized answers must mean the same thing.";
const user = JSON.stringify({question: context.question, customer_language: resolved.plan.customer_language, answer_scope: $('Plan Answer Scope').first().json.output, intents: resolved.plan.intents, allowed_actions: context.allowed_actions, reply_style: context.reply_style});
return [{ json: { system_prompt: system, user_prompt: user } }];

const context = $('Start Draft Request').first().json.context;
const plan = $('Resolve Product Order and Live Facts').first().json.plan;
const draft = $input.first().json.output;
const system = `Translate the supplied English customer-service draft into target_language. Return JSON only: answer_localized. Follow reply_style and preserve the warm, courteous, natural customer-service voice as well as meaning, factual limits, brevity, product numbers, links, and safety wording. Do not add information. If target_language is en, return the English text unchanged.`;
